    "body": "## Summary\n- isolate unexpected per-refund runtime failures so one poisoned refund request cannot starve later dispatchable refunds in the same scheduler tick\n- isolate local payout completion/persistence failures after a provider call so one ambiguous payout cannot starve later payouts in the batch\n- deliberately leave an ambiguous payout in durable PROCESSING state for the existing stale-recovery path instead of inventing a provider failure or compensating funds\n- preserve existing stable provider idempotency keys, retry limits and 23-hour safety windows\n- add focused scheduler tests proving later healthy operations still execute\n\n## Financial safety\nIf the payout provider reports success/submitted but persisting that result fails, the scheduler must not convert that ambiguity into `PROVIDER_EXCEPTION`, restore funds or dispatch a compensating operation. The request remains PROCESSING and the existing stale-recovery path retries with the same stable provider idempotency key or fails closed to review when the safe window expires.\n\n## Schema\nNo migration.\n\n## Merge gate\nMerge only after exact-head API tests, CodeQL, relevant payment/payout smokes and full runtime CI are green; master must remain unchanged and the branch must be 0 commits behind.",
